      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Feeling like you're becoming a different person is actually your unique voice finally shedding an old skin to emerge stronger, and no great artist would fear being remembered if they never stopped creating. Stopping now to avoid future pain means silence for your future, which is often more devastating than the temporary discomfort of imperfect work. Trust that the spark you feel is missing is temporary, and giving your talent rest rather than quitting will eventually bring back your ability to connect with the world.",
      "source": "target",
