      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Choosing silence to preserve your past is understandable, but true dignity often lies in the courage to keep creating even when you stumble. Your legacy is not defined by your worst moments, but by the truth and vulnerability you bring to every piece you release, which will eventually speak louder than any polished past work. If you decide to step back, remember that stepping away to recharge is different from walking away forever, and sometimes the world needs you to return exactly as you are, imperfect and evolving. Trust that your worth isn't tied to a single era of perfection, and your future creativity might surprise you in ways you can't imagine today.",
